  "intro": "Wenatchee belonged to the 82. Vince Conwell drove the Northwest Concrete Cutting car to the main event win and took the full 25. Hector Jr still had the bigger night overall — quick time, a good heat, and 75 points banked in the 68.\n\nUp front it's three cars deep. The 68 leads on 479, Quatsoe has the 8 fifteen back at 464, and Cheth's 23 is another sixteen behind that on 448 — a thirty-one point spread across the top three. Conwell sits fourth on 427, twenty-one off Cheth and twenty-two clear of Strimple's 57.\n\nNew numbers on the board at the Super Oval: D. Eierman rolled the 76 out for the first time and won his heat, leaving with 66. K. Gill got the 65 on the board with 54.\n\nTwo points races left. Points stay with the car, not the driver.",
